Max,

I write on behalf of Callaway Land Partners with respect to comment L-2 in =
the Clark County Public Works first-round review letter dated 10/09/2026 co=
ncerning Desert Sage Ranch Phase 3. Callaway has asked this office to state=
 its position on the applicability of the nonfunctional turf prohibition en=
acted at Nevada AB 356 (2021) and administered within the SNWA service area=
, so that the item may be closed on the resubmittal response matrix without=
 further study.

The nonfunctional turf prohibition, and the 12/31/2026 conversion deadline =
that accompanies it, apply to non-single-family residential properties. Des=
ert Sage Ranch Phase 3 is zoned R-2 detached under Clark County Code Title =
30 and is mapped as single-family residential on the recorded and pending f=
inal map sheets. The subdivision is treated as single-family residential fo=
r regulatory purposes throughout the entitlement record, including the tent=
ative map conditions of approval and the Phase 1/2 map already of record at=
 Book 175, Page 60.

Accordingly, the nonfunctional turf prohibition does not apply to any porti=
on of Phase 3, inclusive of the common-area park parcel. No turf within Pha=
se 3 is subject to conversion under AB 356, and no landscape change is requ=
ired on this ground. The compliance note carried on the L-1 cover sheet cor=
rectly reflects this position and need not be revised.

We ask that Sundial adopt this position in its written response to comment =
L-2 and record the item as closed in the response matrix returned to the Co=
unty. If it assists, this office is prepared to author a short cover letter=
 for inclusion in the resubmittal package restating the foregoing conclusio=
n; please advise whether that would be useful.

Please confirm by reply so we may remove the L-2 comment from the outstandi=
ng items list and inform Callaway that the landscape sheets require no subs=
tantive revision on this account. Garrett is copied for the schedule impact=
 and will follow up separately on the remaining L-series comments.

